# mcp-resources-served - resources/* is served to a conformant client that
# declares the empty clientCapabilities object, and the daemon stays up.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-mcp2026-1-stateless-core AC-13 as corrected. `resources` is a
# member of *ServerCapabilities*, not of ClientCapabilities, whose complete
# member set in MCP 2026-07-28 is `experimental`, `roots`, `sampling`,
# `elicitation` and `extensions`. A conformant client therefore CANNOT declare
# `resources`, so a client-capability gate on it refused every conformant caller
# -- while server/discover advertised `capabilities.resources` and tools/list
# published `_meta.ui.resourceUri` pointing at those very assets. Resources is a
# server capability: a server that offers it just serves it. The -32021 rule
# ("a server MUST NOT rely on capabilities the client has not declared") governs
# capabilities the CLIENT provides, and still gates the Tasks extension.
#
# WHY THIS RUNS AGAINST ze-chaos: Provider mode is where the old code modeled
# "no session" as a nil *session pointer and handed it to every handler, and
# resourcesList/resourcesRead dereferenced it. Provider mode is now the same
# branch as every other caller (internal/component/mcp/resources.go), so this is
# both the R-3 guard -- neither a panic nor a denial may reach a resources call
# -- and the guard against the client-capability gate coming back. A gate
# returning under any name turns each 200 below into a 400.
#
# The final check is the liveness half: after three resource calls the listener
# still answers tools/list, so serving is a per-request verdict and not a crash.

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-chaos --in-process --web :$PORT --mcp :$PORT2 --duration 10s --peers 2 --seed 42 --routes 5 --quiet

# Readiness: GET the POST-only endpoint until it answers 405.
http=wait:seq=1:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/mcp:status=405:contains=method not allowed:timeout=20s

# clientCapabilities is present and EMPTY: the well-formed shape every
# conformant client sends, so this is not a -32602 malformed-_meta case and
# there is nothing left for a capability gate to key on.
tmpfs=reslist.json:terminator=EOF_RESLIST
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"resources/list","params":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28","io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}
EOF_RESLIST

http=post:seq=1:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/mcp:status=200:contains="resultType":"complete":sendfile=reslist.json:header=MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28:header=Mcp-Method: resources/list
http=post:seq=2:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/mcp:status=200:contains=ui://bgp-peer/index.html:sendfile=reslist.json:header=MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28:header=Mcp-Method: resources/list

# resources/read is ungated the same way and returns the asset's real bytes. It
# carries an Mcp-Name mirroring params.uri, so the header contract is satisfied
# too and nothing but the resource lookup decides the outcome.
tmpfs=resread.json:terminator=EOF_RESREAD
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"resources/read","params":{"uri":"ui://bgp-peer/index.html","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28","io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}
EOF_RESREAD

http=post:seq=3:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/mcp:status=200:contains=DOCTYPE html:sendfile=resread.json:header=MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28:header=Mcp-Method: resources/read:header=Mcp-Name: ui://bgp-peer/index.html

# Liveness: the orchestrator survived all three calls and still serves its tools.
tmpfs=list.json:terminator=EOF_LIST
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/list","params":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28","io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}
EOF_LIST

http=post:seq=4:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/mcp:status=200:contains=chaos_status:sendfile=list.json:header=MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28:header=Mcp-Method: tools/list
